nges or extra modules to keep the deal moving. Each promise took 5 points off your Deal Score as delivery risk the committee had to weigh.", insight_eb_late: "You first sat down with an economic buyer (CEO or CFO) in the last round, or never did. Ask yourself what the person who signs could still change at that point.", insight_budget_out: "You ran out of account budget before the cycle ended, so at least one round passed with no engagement at all.", insight_score_not_outcome: "Your Deal Score reached the winning range and the committee still did not sign. A win also needs four of the six stakeholders engaged and a champion who actively supports you: the score alone does not close.", insight_champion_gate: "Your champion did not carry the room. The Supply Chain VP ended below the level of support a win requires, so nobody sold the deal internally when you were not there.", insight_meddic_gaps: "You closed the cycle with MEDDIC gaps. Qualification is built round by round: an element left open in Round 1 does not close by itself later, and each element still open cost 4 points at the close.", dq_1: "To discuss: which stakeholder did you never engage, and what did Apex do with that silence?", dq_2: "To discuss: if Apex cut its price by 20% tomorrow, what would you say to the CFO before saying anything about your own price?" }, es: { title: `DealHunter — Ventas B2B Empresariales`, subtitle: `Cierra un contrato de $780K ARR con GrupoTres frente a un competidor agresivo`, round_label: `Ronda`, period_of: `de`, budget_label: `Presupuesto Restante`, dealscore_label: `Puntaje del Acuerdo`, champion_label: `Fuerza del Champion`, competitive_label: `Posición Competitiva`, meddic_label: `Cobertura MEDDIC`, threads_label: `Stakeholders Contactados`, round1_title: `Ronda 1: Cualificación y Mapeo`, round1_briefing: `El acuerdo se ha estancado tras una demo inicial. GrupoTres lleva 3 semanas en silencio. Necesitas reconectar con el comité de compras, evaluar la calidad del acuerdo 